{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "list_id": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "run": 5,
  "simulation_id": "sim-04",
  "member_id": "kroll-stefan",
  "model": "gpt-5.6-terra",
  "reasoning_effort": "high",
  "prompt": "prompts/physics_committee_terra_round2_v1.md",
  "preferred_configuration": {
    "prize_parts": [
      {
        "ballot_id": "B031",
        "laureates": [
          "Hidetoshi Katori",
          "Jun Ye"
        ],
        "citation": "for the invention and experimental development of optical lattice clocks"
      }
    ]
  },
  "alternatives": [
    "B006",
    "B048"
  ],
  "statement": {
    "case_for": "My configuration is unchanged. Optical lattice clocks remain the strongest combination of a discrete atomic-physics innovation, decisive experimental realization, and demonstrated maturity. The magic-wavelength lattice made it physically possible to interrogate many neutral atoms with strongly suppressed differential light shifts, creating a new regime of coherent, accurate measurement rather than simply refining an existing clock. The resulting capability has been independently reproduced and already enables exceptionally sensitive measurements connected with gravitation and fundamental physics. Katori and Ye remain a focused, complementary attribution: the foundational concept and the experimental development that established the platform's scientific reach.",
    "case_against": "The remaining concern is that the achievement can be misdescribed as cumulative metrological engineering. The citation must instead identify the atomic-physics breakthrough and experimentally established measurement regime, without relying on a prospective redefinition of the second or on future applications. Historical review should also test whether the two-person allocation properly distinguishes indispensable foundational contributions from the broad subsequent international development of lattice clocks.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "member_id": "eriksson-olle",
        "point": "Eriksson favors B026 because it joins a fundamental new classification of matter to a decisive quantum-spin-Hall experimental realization, while recognizing that B031 has unusually clear attribution and reproducibility.",
        "response": "I agree that B026 is a profound theory-experiment achievement and that its scope should be kept narrower than all topological matter. On the common criteria proposed by the chair, however, B031 has the clearer present attribution and a more directly reproducible experimental record. Its advance is also more than improved instrumentation: magic-wavelength confinement established a new controllable atomic measurement regime. The attribution and scope questions surrounding B026 leave it below B031 for me."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "olsson-eva",
        "point": "Olsson favors B018 because qPlus microscopy opened a previously inaccessible molecular-scale observational domain, while warning that its boundary relative to broader atomic-force microscopy and the exact experimental credit require scrutiny.",
        "response": "I share the view that an instrument which makes new phenomena observable can be prize-worthy; that is an important standard for judging B031 as well. But the unresolved separation of qPlus from the wider atomic-force-microscopy history, and the uncertainty over the indispensable roles of Meyer and Gross, are material. For lattice clocks the central physical principle, experimental establishment, and independently demonstrated capability presently form a more coherent and sharply bounded chain."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "mehlig-bernhard",
        "point": "Mehlig favors B001 as a mature, compact fundamental advance, but notes uncertainty about treating several fluctuation relations as one achievement and about the exact priority among Evans, Jarzynski, and Crooks.",
        "response": "The fluctuation theorems are a major conceptual contribution, and I agree that their maturity should not be discounted merely because their experimental confirmation is not the original discovery. Nevertheless, their unity and three-person priority allocation remain substantive questions. B031 supplies an equally mature physical advance with a particularly direct connection between principle, experimental realization, and enduring observational capability."
      }
    ],
    "uncertainties": [
      "Whether historical documentation confirms that Katori and Ye alone represent the indispensable conceptual and experimental contributions to the cited lattice-clock achievement.",
      "Whether the final wording can make clear that the award recognizes a new atomic-physics measurement regime rather than a standards decision or general improvements in timekeeping."
    ],
    "conflict_note": "No candidate-specific conflict is apparent from the supplied profile. I have professional involvement in Swedish quantum-technology networks through WACQT, but the permitted evidence identifies no collaboration, institutional relationship, or other direct connection with the proposed B031 laureates."
  }
}
